# Nous base.manifest — nous-specific additions on top of ariadne's base layer.
#
# Ancestors are discovered automatically by construct/setup.sh (vendored
# from ariadne) via `go list -m all` + replace directives in go.mod. This
# file holds only nous's own contributions; ariadne's base layer is walked
# first as a transitive upstream.
#
# Format: <action> <source-path> [<target-path>]
#
# Actions:
#   symlink   — create symlink (or copy in vendor mode)
#   copy      — copy once (for files that need local modification)
#   scaffold  — create empty directory
#   touch     — create empty file if missing
#   merge     — JSON merge (settings.<layer>.json layered under settings.local.json)

# ── Nous skills ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
symlink   construct/skills/nous-tools    .claude/skills/nous-tools
symlink   construct/skills/charon        .claude/skills/charon
symlink   construct/skills/nous-resolve  .claude/skills/nous-resolve

# ── Makefile ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
symlink   Makefile.nous

# ── Documentation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
copy      README.md           README-NOUS.md

# ── Directory conventions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
scaffold  life
scaffold  memory/ideas/pensive
scaffold  memory/life/travel
scaffold  memory/life/references
scaffold  memory/work/meeting-notes

# ── Plugins (merged from the former nous/plugins/*.manifest pattern) ─────────
# Plugin manifests were a pre-2026-05-19 modular packaging mechanism. With
# selective-plugin support gone (every plugin always applied), the
# modularity adds no operator-visible value, so we inline the contents
# here. Adding new "plugin-shaped" contributions: just append symlink
# entries.

# Gmail plugin — search and read Gmail threads via Charon proxy.
# Requires: charon auth google <email>
symlink   lib/gmail
symlink   cmd/gmail

# Oneshot plugin — single system+user prompt against a local Ollama model.
# Requires: ollama serve running locally (or OLLAMA_HOST set).
symlink   cmd/oneshot
